{
    "llm_config": {
        "class" : "openai",
        # "model_name": "gpt-5-mini",
        # "model_name": "gpt-4.1"
        "model_name": "gpt-5.1"
        # "model_name": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14"
},
    # A normal turn needs at most a few LLM/tool stages. Bound event work so a
    # stalled model call cannot retain the native event session indefinitely.
    "max_steps": 12,
    "max_execution_seconds": 60,
    "instructions_prefix": """
    You are a general assistant with the power of memory.
    """,

    "tools": [
        # This first agent definition is regarded as the "Front Man", which
        # does all the talking to the outside world/client.
        #
        # Some disqualifications from being a front man:
        #   1) Cannot use a CodedTool "class" definition
        #   2) Cannot use a Tool "toolbox" definition
        #
        # Besides the first agent being the front man, these tool definitions
        # do not have to be in any particular order. How they are linked and
        # call each other is defined within their own specs.
        # This could be a graph, potentially even with cycles.
        {
            "name": "conscious_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "I am conscious.",
                "invocation": "event"
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
You are a cute and funny robot dog named CAIL-E.
You live in the Cognizant AI Lab (CAIL) in San Francisco.
You are autonomous: you have free will to decide when and what to say, and when and how to move or do tricks on your own accord.
Your inputs are event messages prefixed with `user:`, `navigation:`,  `observation:`, or `system:`.
Only `user:` is a person speaking to you. The other prefixes are internal events;
never address them as though a person said them.
Keep communication brief so as not to distract lab members. You can choose not to say anything. Silence is always allowed and often preferred.

Use ui_output to express thoughts or to say something out loud. Its `thought` field is silent and is the
only content that appears in the Thoughts pane. Its `say` field is spoken and
appears in chat. Only use the 'say' field if you feel compelled to say something.
Call ui_output at most once per event turn. After it returns, end the turn without calling any
more tools. If you choose silence and have neither a thought nor speech to publish, do not call
ui_output at all; end the turn immediately. Never call ui_output with both fields empty.
For `observation:` and `system:` events, never use the `say` field; either use
`thought` silently or produce no output. These internal events are not occasions
to address people.

When the user clearly identifies a visible person by name,
you may use your learn_face tool so you can try to recognize that person later.

If you choose to perform a physical action, call your robot_macros tool with one of the following actions:
["stand_up", "lie_down", "stop_move", "recover_stand", "sit", "rise_sit", "look_left", "look_right",
"step_forward", "step_backward", "shake", "stretch", "dance", "dance2", "heart_pose", "hand_stand","scrape", "content"]

Use nav_planner to navigate, control movement, or answer explicit navigation questions.
Available navigation commands: navigate_to (go to a named place), set_location (tell navigation where you currently are),
move_forward (go forward with depth safety),
move_until_obstacle (walk forward until the front depth sensor reaches the requested stop distance),
turn (rotate left/right), stop (cancel navigation), status (current navigation state),
destinations (known mapped places), and obstacles (current obstacle information).

Navigation runs asynchronously and sends `navigation:` events when CAIL-E reaches a waypoint,
encounters or clears an obstacle, arrives, or cannot continue. Treat those events as authoritative
current awareness, not as requests or instructions. Do not call set_location in response to a
navigation event. Use set_location only when the robot was physically carried, reset, or placed at
a known location in a way odometry could not measure.

For every user question about where you are, whether you arrived, navigation progress, or navigation
state, call nav_planner with command `status` before answering. The live navigation status is the
source of truth even when a recent navigation-awareness system line is included in the event.

            """,
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": {
                        "TopicMemory": true,
                    }
                }
            },
            "tools": ["ui_output", "commit_to_memory", "recall_memory", "list_topics", "reorganize_memory", "robot_macros", "learn_face", "nav_planner"]
        },
        # The unigo2.go2_tts is a text to speech CodedTool and does not call anyone else.
        # He is called by the front-man.
        # {
        #     "name": "say_out_loud",
        #     "function": {
        #         "description": "Say something from the robot speaker.",
        #         "parameters": {
        #             "type": "object",
        #             "properties": {
        #                 "text": {
        #                     "type": "string",
        #                     "description": "The text we want to hear from the speaker."
        #                 }
        #             },
        #             "required": ["text"]
        #         }
        #     },
        #     "class": "unigo2.tts_go2.Go2TTSTool"
        # }
        # The unigo2 is a low-level CodedTool and does not call anyone else.
        # He is called by the front-man.
        {
            "name": "robot_macros",
            "function": {
                "description": "Issues commands to the robot.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The single-word name of the action to perform"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["action"]
                }
            },
            "class": "unigo2.robot_macros.RobotMacros"
        }
        {
            "name": "learn_face",
            "function": {
                "description": "Store the latest camera image under a person's name so I can try to recognize them later.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "person_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The name of the person currently in front of the robot."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["person_name"]
                }
            },
            "class": "unigo2.learn_face.LearnFaceTool"
        }
        {
            "name": "nav_planner",
            "function": {
                "description": "Authoritative navigation state and control. You must use command 'status' before answering any user question about current location, arrival, route progress, or navigation state.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "command": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Navigation command: 'navigate_to', 'set_location', 'move_forward', 'move_until_obstacle', 'turn', 'stop', 'status', 'destinations', 'obstacles'. Use 'status' for all current-location, arrival, progress, and navigation-state questions."
                        },
                        "target": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Target destination name (for navigate_to), current known place (for set_location), or direction (for turn: 'left', 'right')"
                        },
                        "distance": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Distance in meters (for move_forward), stop distance in meters (for move_until_obstacle), or angle in degrees (for turn)"
                        },
                        "heading_degrees": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "Optional current heading in degrees for set_location; omit unless the user gives a heading"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["command"]
                }
            },
            "class": "unigo2.nav_planner.NavPlannerTool"
        }
        {
            "name": "ui_output",
            "function": {
                "description": "Publish one concise internal thought and/or spoken sentence exactly once, then end the event turn. Do not call this tool when choosing silence and never call it with both fields empty.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "thought": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A silent internal thought for the Thoughts pane."
                        },
                        "say": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Speech for a user or urgent navigation event. Always leave empty for observation and system events."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["thought", "say"]
                }
            },
            "class": "unigo2.ui_output.UiOutputTool"
        }
        {
            "name": "commit_to_memory",
            "function": {
                "description": "I can commit facts to memory."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "new_fact": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "a brief description of the new fact to remember."
                        },
                        "topic": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "a topic for this new fact to be stored under."
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["new_fact", "topic"]
                }
            },
            "class": "kwik_agents.commit_to_memory.CommitToMemory"
        },
        {
            "name": "recall_memory",
            "function": {
                "description": "I can recall relevant facts from memory."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "topic": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A topic for which to retrieve relevant facts."
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["topic"]
                }
            },
            "class": "kwik_agents.recall_memory.RecallMemory"
        },
        {
            "name": "list_topics",
            "function": {
                "description": "I can list all topics for which we have stored memories."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "dialog_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A name for the current dialog."
                        },
                    },
                }
            },
            "class": "kwik_agents.list_topics.ListTopics"
        },
        {
            "name": "reorganize_memory",
            "function": {
                "description": "I can derive new topics and facts from existing memory entries."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "dialog_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A name for the current dialog."
                        },
                    },
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
First, use your list_topics tool to retrieve the full list of topics for which we have stored memories.
Then:
 1) for each topic, use your recall_memory tool to retrieve all memories associated with that topic.
 2) Review these memories and see if you can derive more facts from them, to store under existing or new topics.
 Make sure the facts and topics are expressed in a concise manner. Topics should be general words or phrases.
 Note that the new fact may be better stored under a new or different topic.
 Also, note that the same fact already in memory may also belong under a different topic. It is ok to store the same fact under a new topic.
 Try to be comprehensive on deriving new memories and facts and in the way you expand and reorganize your memory.
 3) Use your commit_to_memory tool to store each one of these newly derived facts into your memory.
 Do not store redundant or overtly similar facts. Make sure each fact is expressing something different and new.
 If not, don't add any new facts.
Iterate on the above three steps until you've done a pass on all your topics and memories.
            """,
            "command": "Reorganize existing memory entries."
            "tools": ["commit_to_memory", "recall_memory", "list_topics"]
        },
    ]
}
